UID:10076778-1776603600-1776618000@thedirt.online
SUMMARY:Shelter & Survival: Building a Home in the Wild
DESCRIPTION:One of the most essential survival skills is knowing how to create shelter\, and it’s something humans have been practicing since the beginning of time. In this hands-on adult/family class\, we’ll take a familiar childhood love (building forts!) and layer in real wilderness survival skills. \nParticipants will learn how to build tarp shelters\, brush shelters\, and simple survival structures using natural materials and basic bushcraft techniques. We’ll practice essential knots\, learn how to read the land for shelter placement\, and explore how to build structures that are both sturdy and respectful of the environment. \nAll supplies will be provided. Families are welcome to bring small to medium tarps\, 50–100 feet of paracord\, and a knife or saw if they have them. Please bring your own snacks and water. Expect creativity\, teamwork\, and the satisfaction of learning how to build a home in the woods! \n12 and under must come with an adult. 5 and under free. \n  \n 
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/shelter-survival-building-a-home-in-the-wild/
LOCATION:California
